Jenkins Commands and Scenarios
🔧 Jenkins Setup and Configuration
•	jenkins --version
→ Check Jenkins version installed.
•	sudo systemctl start jenkins
→ Start Jenkins service.
•	sudo systemctl stop jenkins
→ Stop Jenkins service.
•	sudo systemctl status jenkins
→ Check Jenkins service status.
•	sudo systemctl enable jenkins
→ Enable Jenkins to start on boot.
•	sudo cat /var/lib/jenkins/secrets/initialAdminPassword
→ Get initial admin password after installation.
📁 Jenkins Job Management (CLI and UI)
•	jenkins-cli.jar -s http://localhost:8080/ create-job <job-name> < config.xml
→ Create a new job from config file.
•	jenkins-cli.jar -s http://localhost:8080/ delete-job <job-name>
→ Delete a Jenkins job.
•	jenkins-cli.jar -s http://localhost:8080/ build <job-name>
→ Trigger a build for a job.
•	jenkins-cli.jar -s http://localhost:8080/ disable-job <job-name>
→ Disable a job.
•	jenkins-cli.jar -s http://localhost:8080/ enable-job <job-name>
→ Enable a job.
🔁 Jenkins Pipeline and Build Commands
•	pipeline syntax
→ Used in UI to generate pipeline script snippets.
•	agent any
→ Used in Jenkinsfile to run on any available agent.
•	steps { ... }
→ Defines the build steps in a pipeline.
•	post { success { ... } failure { ... } }
→ Post-build actions based on result.
🔐 Jenkins User and Security Management
•	Manage Jenkins > Configure Global Security
→ Enable security and configure authentication.
•	Manage Jenkins > Manage Users
→ Add or remove users.
•	Manage Jenkins > Configure Credentials
→ Add credentials for Git, Docker, etc.
📦 Jenkins Plugin Management
•	Manage Jenkins > Manage Plugins
→ Install, update, or remove plugins.
•	jenkins-cli.jar -s http://localhost:8080/ install-plugin <plugin-name>
→ Install plugin via CLI.
•	jenkins-cli.jar -s http://localhost:8080/ list-plugins
→ List installed plugins.
📜 Jenkins Logs and Monitoring
•	/var/log/jenkins/jenkins.log
→ Main Jenkins log file.
•	Manage Jenkins > System Log
→ View logs from the UI.
•	Manage Jenkins > Load Statistics
→ Monitor system load and performance.
🧪 Jenkins Testing and Debugging
•	echo 'Hello World'
→ Simple shell step to test pipeline.
•	sh 'exit 1'
→ Simulate a failed build step.
•	archiveArtifacts artifacts: '**/*.jar'
→ Archive build artifacts.
